* text=auto

# ref/ holds the offline seeders' output - up to ~15MB of minified JSON on a
# single line. -text keeps git from line-ending-normalising an opaque blob,
# -diff stops `git diff` / `git show` / GitHub from rendering one into a
# terminal, a PR view, or an agent's context window, and -merge turns a
# conflict into a loud failure instead of a silent mangle. Declared as a glob
# so a new seeder output is covered before anyone remembers to add it here.
ref/*.json -text -diff -merge linguist-generated=true

# ...except the files under ref/ a human writes and a reviewer has to read:
# the provenance manifests, the hand-curated vendor exclusions (each row
# carries its own evidence), and the hand-maintained hint/cooldown/sheet
# lists. These are small, and making them unreadable would defeat the point.
# eol=lf rather than text=auto on the manifests specifically: Program.cs's
# SerializeManifest forces LF, and VendorOfferManifestTests compares the
# shipped file's bytes to its output. text=auto would hand a Windows clone
# (core.autocrlf=true) a CRLF working copy and fail that test on unmodified
# code. CI stays green either way - GitHub's windows image sets autocrlf=input
# - so the breakage would land on a contributor's machine, not the runner.
ref/*_manifest.json text eol=lf diff merge -linguist-generated
ref/vendor_offer_exclusions.json text=auto diff merge -linguist-generated
ref/acquisition_hints_seed.json text=auto diff merge -linguist-generated
ref/daily_cooldown_items.json text=auto diff merge -linguist-generated
ref/recipe_sheet_items.json text=auto diff merge -linguist-generated

# ...and the three large seeds that are pretty-printed rather than minified.
# The glob above assumes seeder output is one opaque line, which is true of
# vendor_offers.json and item_name_seed.json but not of these: at two-space
# indent they diff line-by-line and auto-merge like any other text file, and
# recipe_search_seed.json and recipes_seed.json ARE seeder output, so they say
# so - linguist-generated collapses them in a PR view by default while diff and
# merge keep them readable when someone opens them. mystic_forge_recipes.json is
# hand-curated on top of its seeded rows, so it is not marked generated.
# eol=lf, not text=auto, for the same reason as the manifests - and measured
# the hard way: ShippedSeedManifest sha-pins the two recipe seeds, and the
# first CI run with text=auto failed both pins because the Windows runner
# checks out CRLF (the earlier claim here that GitHub's image uses
# autocrlf=input was wrong - PR #184 run 32988578177 is the counterexample).
# The seeder writes LF; eol=lf hands every clone the bytes the digest names.
ref/mystic_forge_recipes.json text eol=lf diff merge -linguist-generated
ref/recipe_search_seed.json text eol=lf diff merge linguist-generated=true
ref/recipes_seed.json text eol=lf diff merge linguist-generated=true

# Shell scripts run from Git Bash, where core.autocrlf=true otherwise hands
# the working tree CRLF copies. Git Bash tolerates a CRLF shebang, so this is
# not about the scripts failing to start; it is that a CR rides along on every
# unquoted capture and comparison downstream, which fails somewhere far from
# the cause. These scripts now bootstrap and refresh data in throwaway
# worktrees, so they get checked out fresh far more often than they get edited.
*.sh text eol=lf
